<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Drina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Drina is a river of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, about 346 km long, formed by the Tara and Piva and flowing north into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a>. For much of its course it marks the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>. The Ottoman bridge at Višegrad, built for Mehmed Pasha Sokolović in 1577, inspired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivo-andric">Ivo Andrić</a>'s novel The Bridge on the Drina.</p></div>
